speechtext:
I should have Indicated that I propose introducing an amendment. I completely forgot. I am glad my hon. friend has spoken of it. I think the point is covered now. I would ask my colleague, the Secretary of State, if he would be good enough to move that in line 36, after the word "certificate", the following should be inserted:
The party against whom it is produced may require the attendance of the analyst for the purpose of cross-examination;
That is done at the request of the Canadian Pharmaceutical Manufacturers Association who thought that this should be in. This is put in so that there will be no misunderstanding.
